     2	
     3	Source: `V025-ENGINE-STAGE2-AUDIT-CLAUDE-OPUS-2026-09-08.md` — verdict `ENGINE_FAITHFUL=NO` on four blockers around a faithful physics core; 14/102 tests tautological; five producers only reachable from tests. All items below are binding for engine stage 4 (not started at the time of writing).
     4	
     5	1. **B1 — treatment H/SH is a no-op.** The runner never constructs `InterruptionEvent`s, so `useful_availability ≡ decoding_availability` and 10 of 31 settings are bit-identical duplicates. FIX: interruption events are built from the common event ledger (62 ms same-satellite beam change, 142 ms satellite change; initial entry logged without blackout; overlaps unioned and clipped once, per decision 5 of stage 1) and passed to `score_setting`; KAT: on a world with ≥ 1 handover, `a-γ0 ≠ a-γH` in useful bits and `a-γS ≠ a-γSH`; the setting-duplicate test asserts all 31 receipts are pairwise distinct on a synthetic world with handovers.
     6	2. **B2 — factor arms cannot measure component marginals (design CHANGE).** The set decoder's score for FULL/DROP arms is the **sum of the declared targets**, not the exact realised objective: S(config) = C1(config) + C2(config) + C3(config), each the declared target in bits computed by the oracle from the same nominal physics (C1 whole-network difference surplus + Φ; C2 three-offset forecasts with −κ; C3 = interaction share per decision item 5 / Shapley for sets). DROP_Cx removes exactly one term inside the **same selector class and the same catalogue**; `DROP_C3` = no interaction term (joint search kept); an additional `UNI` arm = unilateral-only search with all three terms is reported separately (search value ≠ interaction value); `S_UNI` (stage-4 item 11) is the iterated exact-unilateral comparator. The exact-F oracle is a **ceiling arm** (U1/J1/union certificates), never a factor arm. Marginals are measured on the realised pooled endpoint ΣB/ΣE, never on nominal scores. KATs: on a synthetic world with a constructed non-zero interaction, FULL and DROP_C3 select different configurations and the realised marginal equals the hand-computed value; with zero interaction they coincide; DROP_C1/DROP_C2 differ from FULL on fixtures where the dropped term is decisive.
