     8	4. **B4 — runner cannot execute a real world.** Bounded catalogue (stage-2 decision 4) with an explicit size guard; a user with zero legal candidates receives the null action (unserved) and is excluded from the product — the catalogue never silently collapses to {BASE}; KAT: one user with no legal candidate → 11 non-BASE arms still differ from BASE on a fixture where they should, and a receipt field counts null-action users.
