     1	# V025 — controller decisions after the stage-4c real-anchor gate (2026-09-08 ≈ 21:50 UTC; before any formal successor outcome)
     2	
     3	Trigger: stage 4c stopped at the mandatory real-anchor gate: the a-r0 FULL selector on the quarantined world chose a 100-user coalition; the runner then tried an exact Shapley validation over 2^100 subsets and failed closed; the timing table read catalogue 3.0 s, stage 1 36.5 s, stage-2 forecasts 17.8 s, selection 0.01 s — 59.7 s to failure against the 10 s selection budget.
     4	
     5	1. **Coalition credit rule (clarifies contract v1 §B5 / v1.5 §2):** the set-score decomposition dᵢ (|A| evaluations) and Ψ_A (one evaluation) are always computed — O(|A|), never 2^|A|. Per-user Shapley credit is **reporting only and only for |A| ≤ 4**; for larger selected coalitions the receipt records Ψ_A at set level with `credit_split = NOT_COMPUTED_LARGE_SET`. No selection or validation step may depend on a per-user split. The 2^|A| validation is removed.
